<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · concept</p><h1 class="enc-title">Extraterritoriality</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as extraterritorial</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Extraterritoriality is the exemption of foreigners from the jurisdiction of local courts, so that they are tried under their own country's law. Imposed on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a> by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unequal-treaties">unequal treaties</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/opium-wars">Opium Wars</a>, it became a symbol of foreign encroachment on Chinese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/extraterritoriality.jpg" alt="Extraterritoriality" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Etan J. Tal · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SanPaoloFuoriLeMura1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
